> /* GC500 3D proof, v6.90 (Andrew Fisher, 27 Sep 2026: "high tech attention … more detail, more quality … smoother and
>    clearer"). Google Photorealistic 3D Tiles (Map Tiles API) streamed by CesiumJS for the current view only; the Google key
>    comes from the dashboard service at runtime (never written into this file); Google's attribution stays on screen.
>    Cesium's own buttons are off (their bindings need string eval, which the service's policy refuses).
>    New in v6.90:
>    - SHARPER: each screen draws at its own pixel density, detail is fetched finer at rest, and anti-aliasing (MSAA and
>      FXAA) is on.
>    - SMOOTHER: the camera coasts, tiles along a flight are preloaded, and requests that a move makes stale are culled.
>    - THE JOB ON THE MODEL: every unit the master plan places, and what the other sheets draw, stands on the 3D model as
>      a pin in its trade's colour. Tap one for what it is; search a reference to fly to it.
>    - N, E, S, W: a compass that faces the camera any way, and a slow orbit round what you are looking at.
>    Rendering is on demand (nothing is drawn while the camera is still) and stops when the tab is hidden. */
